WEBVTT

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.060
You'll win?

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.740
Interesting theory, Kyoto Fushimi 
first-year Kishigami Komari.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:08.860
You've kept up well so far.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.610
And on top of that, you sure do talk a lot.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.360
Izumida-san, let me hear 
you shout "abs" more!

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.120
I want to see more!

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.870
I want to see them whip back and forth!

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.500
I want to hear the passionate 
braying of your muscles!

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:31.610
Contract and release. They repeat 
that action over and over.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:35.550
Magnificently and proudly, thousands 
and tens of thousands of times.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.930
Muscles are beautiful!

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:42.250
The process by which you develop 
your muscles is important.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.640
Muscles that are raised 
carefully are high quality.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.790
Their appearance, feel, 
elasticity, and durability...

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.150
All their properties shine fantastically.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.770
But muscles raised roughly 
are crude and disconnected.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:00.450
They possess no shred of dignity 
and feel like mud to the touch.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:07.040
Muscles need innate quality and 
a maestro to raise them well.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:13.880
I can't stand it!

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.260
Izumida-san!

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.840
Your muscles are beautiful!

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.850
You are the greatest maestro!

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:24.980
And I am the gourmet who will consume them!

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:37.490
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:00.970
<i>Line.13 He Who Carries Guilt</i>

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:00.970
Pushed past their limits, 
muscle fibers are torn.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:04.370
I believe muscles are finally finished then.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:08.080
And with these fingertips, I will touch

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:11.370
the highest-quality dish you've prepared.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.340
<i>Kishigami Komari...</i>

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.250
<i>Is he trying to knock me out of the race?</i>

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:20.600
<i>On the first day, he left the rear and 
caught up to the front with Midousuji.</i>

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.050
<i>He may be an unknown, but he's strong.</i>

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.180
In other words, Kyoto Fushimi has 
revealed their secret weapon.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.850
Which means that now, it can be achieved.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.560
Last year's revenge, which I swore 
I'd have from the bottom of my heart!

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.450
It seems Midousuji-kun carefully planned

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.820
to add you to the lineup just 
before the race started.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:44.260
Yes. He said everything's 
going according to plan.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:49.540
And that I wouldn't need to restrain 
myself once the race started.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:55.640
I thought the round-eyed guy
 would go after them

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:59.060
so they could crush Izumida-san together.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.680
Yeah, but he's not moving.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.910
Does that mean they've 
given up on the sprint?

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:04.510
No.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.760
They deliberately caught up to us 
five kilometers before the line.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:12.640
They care about this race, so if they
 sent that Kishigami guy, then...

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:15.770
Hey, Midousuji.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.060
Huh?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:22.860
At the very least, you must think 
that first-year will beat Touichirou.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.610
What? Beat Izumida-san?

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:27.990
Well...

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.880
I wasn't expecting him to go.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.250
But he'll win.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.090
Then it will be the same as last year.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:46.010
Champion Hakone Academy's ace sprinter
 defeated by a first-year.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:49.890
Once he loses, he'll be completely crushed.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.310
Mr. Revenge Lashes.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.400
<i>He's pulling ahead.</i>

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.980
<i>His form isn't just beautiful.</i>

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:05.360
<i>His pedaling is driving his sprocket
 with almost perfect efficiency.</i>

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:10.650
<i>Despite his strange appearance, he's skilled 
at the fundamentals of riding a bicycle.</i>

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:13.290
<i>He's fast!</i>

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.160
<b>2 km to Road Race
 Second Day Sprint Line</b>

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.120
They've passed the two-kilometer line!

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.710
Hakone Academy's Izumida 
is slowly falling behind!

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:22.800
Izumida-san!

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.020
Aren't you going to get revenge 
for last year's second day?

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:31.060
More! Let me hear your 
muscles bray "abs" more!

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.680
Revenge, huh?

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:36.060
It seems I've given you the wrong impression.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.220
What?

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:39.730
Midousuji.

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:43.000
It sounds like you've gotten 
the wrong impression.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:46.780
Touichirou said "revenge."

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:51.870
But he wasn't talking about your 
sprint against Shinkai-san last year.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:55.670
We crushed the first day. We're doing well.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.330
But for him, he's still...

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:02.090
Last year's loser.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:07.720
The revenge he seeks is for 
Hakone Academy's defeat.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.480
That's a different kind of resolve.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.890
That's why he can't lose, 
no matter who he's against.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.090
He's about to become the fastest spear.

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:23.190
Kishigami-kun, do you know what 
it means when I zip up my jersey?

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:26.690
Huh? What it means when 
you zip up your jersey?

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.900
I can't see your muscles anymore.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.570
There's no other meaning.

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:35.240
<b>1500 m to Road Race
 Second Day Sprint Line</b>

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:35.240
There's 1500 meters left to 
the second day's sprint line!

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:38.680
"Watch out for the zipper 
of Kanagawa's fastest man."

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.210
They used to say that about me.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:45.240
I zip up my jersey just like this

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.420
when I go all out!

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:57.030
Abs!

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:02.900
That's the face of someone who's
lost their lead in an instant.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.860
Try to keep up, first-year. I'm going faster.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:10.900
This acceleration isn't fast 
enough to defeat Hakone Academy's

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:14.260
man wearing #4, the ace sprinter!

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:17.020
I wear #4!

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:20.030
And being the captain of Hakone Academy

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:23.380
is an unimaginably heavy responsibility!

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:30.020
You're dividing each year 
into groups A through D?

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:31.180
That's right, Murakami.

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:34.180
And at the start of every month, we'll hold
 promotion and relegation races.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:36.730
You'll assign the first-years to groups.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:37.930
Takadajou, assist him.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:39.430
Yes, sir!

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:42.740
It's been two months since 
the Inter-High ended.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:46.320
Izumida's doing a surprisingly 
good job as captain.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.020
Yeah.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.400
Thank you!

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.560
But being the captain after 
Hakone Academy loses...

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:55.160
He looks calm, but I'm 
sure he's freaking out.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:56.900
I feel sorry for him.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:00.120
Yeah. And that's not all.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:05.460
Yeah. He's a prime candidate for #4.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.630
<b>Hakone Academy Bicycle Racing Club</b>

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:12.730
Has the captain position really been decided?

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:15.010
What do you mean? Do you 
have a problem with him?

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:18.220
It's just that Hakone Academy's captain

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:21.560
has historically always been 
a climber or all-rounder.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:26.220
Supposedly, it's because sprinters can't
 issue instructions at the end of the race.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.150
So it should be Kuroda-san or Manami?

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:33.530
I'm just saying, don't you 
think that would be better?

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:38.520
Apparently, it's the first time the captain 
of Hakone Academy has been a sprinter.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.990
<b>Meeting In Progress
 Do Not Enter</b>

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:48.600
I thought about not saying anything, 
but there's no point in hiding it.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:54.150
You pay attention to your surroundings, 
and your instructions are accurate.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:56.450
I think you make a good captain.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.350
But there's a strange atmosphere 
spreading throughout the team.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:06.740
An atmosphere of doubt that we can really 
win with a sprinter as our captain.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:10.800
A raging first-year even directly 
appealed to Fukutomi-san.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.340
He said we couldn't win the Inter-High 
like this and demanded we switch captains.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:15.990
I told him not to be stupid—

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.570
I know, Yuki.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:22.970
First-year Murakami told me 
directly the other day.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:24.190
That bastard!

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:25.290
Yuki-chan.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.310
It's okay, Yuki.

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:30.110
I've actually steeled my resolve.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:32.630
If the team is divided now, 
we can't become stronger.

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:37.320
Yuki, I need you to do something for me.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:40.970
The captain's position...

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.020
Wait a minute.

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:50.320
You carry that pride more than 
anyone else, Izumida Touichirou!

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.610
I lost the first day's sprint!

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:58.450
If there's a reason Hakone Academy 
lost the Inter-High this year,

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:02.140
it's because I failed to take the 
first day's green number tag!

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:03.850
That start was everything!

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:07.090
I'm the one who stained our honor, Yuki!

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:08.790
That's irrelevant!

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.920
You have to stop clinging to the past!

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.800
If there's no sprinter captain in our
 team's history, then you write that history!

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:18.450
Your earnestness is your strength!

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:20.930
Just chip away at it, and overturn
 their assumptions!

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:23.930
I've thought about it countless times.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:27.930
But it's guilt.

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:34.580
A guilty person can't lead others.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.430
That's how it is, Yuki.

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:40.570
You should be the captain.

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:52.000
I'm going to tell the others 
officially tomorrow.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:01.000
<i>This is my last day as captain.</i>

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:03.190
Do you have a minute?

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:07.680
If you have some time,
 why don't we go for a ride?

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:09.400
Ashikiba...

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:19.190
This may be the first time we've 
ridden together like this, Ashikiba.

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:21.490
Yeah, Tou-chan.

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:22.820
<i>Tou-chan?</i>

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.430
<i>Ah, short for Touichirou.</i>

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:28.040
<i>I forgot, this guy's a little odd.</i>

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:32.390
<i>I'm sure he's trying to 
cheer me up in his own way.</i>

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.520
<i>But he's wasting his time.</i>

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:39.210
<i>I feel sorry for him, but I'm leaving 
as soon as I hear what he has to say.</i>

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:42.510
It's only the beginning of October, 
but the nights are already cold—

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:43.470
Cheer up!

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.490
<i>He's taking the direct approach!</i>

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:47.260
Sure...

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:49.270
Look! You can see the view!

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.270
Yeah. This is an observation platform.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.510
<i>Why did Shinkai-san</i>

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:57.070
<i>choose this man for the core team of 
the next generation of Hakone Academy?</i>

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:00.630
Shinkai-san used to bring 
me here all the time!

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:02.330
Yeah. Me, too.

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:03.870
Like when I was depressed!

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:06.030
It was the same for me. I know.

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:14.750
From now on, we have to bring people here...

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:18.460
Depressed underclassmen, to this place.

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:22.010
After all, we're becoming upperclassmen.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.510
Yeah, you're right.

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:29.650
<i>I'm surprised he actually 
thinks about these things.</i>

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:31.680
You know, I...

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:34.020
Can I be serious for a second?

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.840
Huh? Uh, sure.

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:38.570
<i>Was he not being serious before?</i>

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:42.110
I moved here from Chiba at 
the end of middle school.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.820
I joined Hakone Academy with zero friends.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:48.950
I joined the team since I brought 
my bike, and they had a club.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.080
It turned out they were strong.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.040
Who the hell are you?

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.540
You're huge!

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:59.000
Arakita-san was scary, I kept growing,
 and practice was hard.

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:01.090
I couldn't keep up.

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:04.590
At some point, I became the laundry boy.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:10.810
But Fukutomi-san and 
Shinkai-san cheered me up.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.080
It made me really happy.

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:17.310
But I failed to meet their 
expectations when I got my chance.

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:20.770
I was so impatient when things 
didn't go the way I wanted

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.980
that I did something you should never do.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:26.250
<i>That was a huge issue within the team.</i>

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:31.240
<i>And the result was a 
permanent ban from racing.</i>

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:35.550
I don't think I had to win that race.

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:38.900
They just wanted me to finish in the 
top nine and gain some confidence.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:44.170
Arakita-san told me later that's what 
Shinkai-san and Fukutomi-san wanted.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:47.210
But I put that pressure on myself.

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:50.810
My need to win turned out badly.

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.930
Earlier, in the club room, 
you said you felt guilt.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:57.940
If that's guilt,

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:02.110
then I carry more guilt than anyone.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.420
And probably...

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:09.590
Oh, I'm not talking about me.

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:14.830
But I think people who don't 
carry guilt shouldn't lead others.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:20.180
Wait, does it sound like
 I'm lecturing you right now?

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:21.290
I'm not, though!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.630
I was just telling you my life story!

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:26.280
I doubt your resolve can be shaken.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:28.770
I just wanted you to cheer up.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:32.260
Yeah, I know.

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:40.150
Since you became captain, I feel 
like you haven't said "abs" once.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:55.370
<b>Hakone Academy</b>

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:48.360
<i>I talked to Yuki. I talked to Fukutomi-san.</i>

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:51.080
<i>But after hearing it from Ashikiba, 
I finally realized something.</i>

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:55.370
<i>Since I became captain,
 I haven't said "abs" once.</i>

00:14:56.130 --> 00:14:58.100
<i>I haven't talked to you...</i>

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.850
<i>Andy, Frank.</i>

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:05.450
<i>To you. To myself.</i>

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:09.460
<i>They're telling me to do it.</i>

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:12.260
<i>That retreating isn't fighting.</i>

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:14.330
<i>Is this my limit?</i>

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.240
<i>If it isn't,</i>

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:21.230
<i>then I should take my guilt and failures and
 turn them into the strength to move forward.</i>

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.440
Abs!

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.370
I placed second at the Minegayama race.

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:29.030
Fukutomi-san got mad at me again.

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:34.910
<i>Second place means he kept working hard 
during his permanent ban from racing.</i>

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:40.370
<b>Hakone Academy</b>

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:39.000
<i>Despite the guilt he carries, 
he's moving forward.</i>

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:40.370
<i>Then I should as well.</i>

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:43.420
Stop looking back and move forward.

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:47.880
<i>Those eyes... He's back.</i>

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:52.630
Touichirou...

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:56.540
Sorry, Yuki. I'll try again.

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:58.680
If there's no precedent,
 then I'll overthrow the past.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.480
If the team isn't satisfied, 
I'll push them aside.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:04.740
My greatest goal is to reclaim 
our throne at the Inter-High.

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:05.860
That's the spirit.

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:08.340
Will you help me, Yuki?

00:16:08.340 --> 00:16:10.280
Yeah, of course.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:11.350
And...

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:13.240
Takuto.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.160
Yeah.

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:17.050
We'll train harder than anyone else.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:19.410
We'll have more passion than anyone else.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:21.370
We'll face forward and advance!

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:24.170
We are the champions, Hakone Academy!

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:29.210
I'm going even faster.

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:31.350
The man wearing #4

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:34.680
and bearing the captain's responsibility
 can go faster than this.

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:39.780
<i>Go, Touichirou.</i>

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:43.560
<i>Show them what you've built in the past year.</i>

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:49.020
<i>I knew there'd come a moment when 
you could atone for your guilt.</i>

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:51.070
That moment is now, Tou-chan.

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:53.070
<i>Run!</i>

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:55.730
<i>I know now why Shinkai-san and Fukutomi-san</i>

00:16:55.730 --> 00:17:00.520
<i>chose Ashikiba for the core team of 
the new generation of Hakone Academy.</i>

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:05.620
<i>He is strong both physically and mentally.</i>

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:09.460
<i>They knew I was carrying guilt.</i>

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:13.670
<i>That's why they told me to 
move forward through him.</i>

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:16.300
<i>Thank you, Yuki, Takuto.</i>

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:20.010
<i>Thanks to you, I made it this far.</i>

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:23.390
Experiencing pain, bearing guilt,

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:26.690
and carrying an unbeatable passion 
in my heart, I now become

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.980
the fastest spear!

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:33.870
He's so fast!

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:35.930
That's how fast Hakone Academy's #4 can go!

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:36.580
Light...

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.410
I think I just saw light!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.450
But...

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.870
No, no...

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:47.080
I can't see him anymore.

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:49.050
His muscles!

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:50.090
In that case,

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:52.460
I'll have to use these!

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:56.710
Eyewear...

00:17:56.710 --> 00:17:59.980
They protect your eyes 
from UV rays and rocks.

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:01.930
But that's not all.

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:07.860
Polarized glasses remove reflections, 
allowing you to see vivid sights.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:14.070
Down to the tiniest detail, 
they increase the vibrant glow...

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:16.950
Of those sights! Those muscles!

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:19.530
It's like a field of flowers!

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:26.410
And beyond that field, I see 
seductively glowing muscles!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:27.960
Muscles!

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:33.670
They'd make anyone want to race 
through a field of flowers!

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:34.890
What's going on?

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:37.750
He suddenly started going faster 
the moment he put on his eyewear!

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.420
Is that even possible?

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:40.930
Maybe.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:41.550
What?

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:44.660
They say more than 85% 
of the information people

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:47.560
use to make decisions during 
exercise is visual information.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:50.920
And if that eyewear drastically 
changes that information,

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:54.310
then it's entirely possible that 
it could affect his movements!

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:55.180
Flowers! Muscles!

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:55.720
Flowers! Muscles!

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:56.610
Flowers! Muscles! Flowers!

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:56.900
Muscles!

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:57.860
Flowers!

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.490
<i>What? But I was so far ahead of him.</i>

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:03.870
<i>What did he do?</i>

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:06.650
I can see them so clearly!

00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:07.540
So close!

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:09.790
A field of muscles!

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.420
<i>A field of muscles?</i>

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:15.150
Muscles are most beautiful 
when they're in motion.

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:17.830
Sweat, contraction, tension...

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:23.180
And the movement of these muscles 
during this ultimate sprint battle...

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:25.680
I may never get a chance to see them again!

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:28.120
<i>I'm sorry, Midousuji-san.</i>

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:29.850
<i>You told me not to put on my eyewear until...</i>

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:33.730
Wear them once you're within 
a kilometer of the line.

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:35.960
Save your secret weapon until the very end.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:37.440
<i>I know you told me not to.</i>

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.860
<i>But I put them on more than a kilometer away!</i>

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:47.990
<i>The stronger his opponent, the more 
his pressure rises. He's keeping up.</i>

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.370
A field... of muscles...

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:55.000
I know, Andy, Frank.

00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:57.590
But I won't quail.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.880
Overwhelming victory has simply 
changed into a close battle.

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:03.200
Huh? Didn't I tell you earlier?

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:05.660
I can tell from the 
movements of your muscles.

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:08.260
I'm going to win this battle.

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:11.020
If the movement of my muscles 
decided the race's outcome,

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.850
then I wouldn't have lost last year.

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:16.130
Don't you know?

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:20.900
In road racing, the one who overcomes 
unexpected difficulties wins.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:29.660
He's keeping up with Izumida!

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:33.240
Maybe I'll root for #116, Hironishi!

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:34.370
Kyoto Fushimi, Hironishi!

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:35.520
You can do it, Hironishi!

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:36.750
You're amazing, Hironishi!

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.410
What a shame.

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:40.300
Since you changed your roster 
just before the race,

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:42.510
everyone's getting your name wrong.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.130
Huh? I don't care about that.

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:49.430
I've never felt the voices 
of others made me stronger.

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:53.940
<b>Sprint 1 km Line Crossed
 14 Izumida
 116 Kishigami
 0 Second Difference</b>

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:56.600
What? A zero second difference 
with one kilometer to go?

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:57.490
Wow...

00:20:57.490 --> 00:21:00.550
N-No, he works surprisingly hard.

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:01.400
He's all right.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:04.110
Damn it, Izumida-san!

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:09.370
<i>He's strong.</i>

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:17.210
<i>After all, I'm the one who 
taught him to unleash himself.</i>

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:17.210
<b>Arashiyama
 Bicycle Park</b>

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:23.090
You were here yesterday, too.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:26.450
Do you like road racing?

00:21:27.860 --> 00:21:28.760
Muscles...

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:32.010
Sorry, it's nothing.

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:08.640
Hey, Ashikiba. I won this at the 
arcade on my way home yesterday.

00:23:08.640 --> 00:23:09.720
You can have it.

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:11.950
You're always forgetting your 
phone, so stick it on there.

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:15.060
It's so cute.

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:16.620
Thanks, Yuki-chan.

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:19.460
Yuki, you've been taking 
a lot of detours lately.

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:20.930
Not all the time.

00:23:20.930 --> 00:23:22.260
You're so strict, Touichirou.

00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:23.250
Who are you, my mom?

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:25.500
Huh? No, he's Tou-chan.

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:28.280
And Ashikiba, you're a third-year now.

00:23:28.280 --> 00:23:30.120
Don't forget things so often.

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:32.800
How many times are you going to 
borrow my textbooks this week?

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:35.120
He really is like my mom.

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:35.940
Right?

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT LINE  Heart's Wrapping, Heart's Case</i>

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:51.500
<b>Don't miss the next episode</b>
